      <adr-check>Compliant: ADR-002 (no plugins), ADR-010 (Path C applied — concrete class, SDK-interface test seam), ADR-013 (no AI dependency), ADR-024 (dual-field write; sprk_signal.sprk_regardingrecordtype is TEXT not a lookup, documented adaptation), ADR-028 (owner-approved exception). No new package, no new endpoint, no new background work; dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive: zero vulnerable (checked after both the first implementation and the rework).</adr-check>
    </quality-gates>
    <test-rows>sprk_signal ae5d9784-f2bf-f111-a05c-0022482913fc ("ONTOLOGY DEV TEST 030 - writer schema sanity check", via Dataverse MCP, first implementation) — deleted. sprk_signal created by the LIVE seam test's passing matter-subject test ("ONTOLOGY DEV TEST 030 - seam sanity check") — deleted by the seam's own DisposeAsync (operator client). Verified by direct query after the seam run: 0 rows matching 'ONTOLOGY DEV TEST%' remain.</test-rows>
