  <completion-r2 date="2026-10-04">
    <summary>
      Second independent review returned "pass with findings" (R1-R15) against the first rework above. All
      addressed; disposition per R-number is in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/030-signal-writer-progress.md
      "Second independent review" section. Highlights: R1 (High) — the reconcile path now re-selects and
      re-checks owningbusinessunit (no extra round trip) via a new shared EnsureOwningBusinessUnitMatches
      helper used on BOTH the create-verify and reconcile paths; a read-back that throws after a successful
      create is wrapped as its own escalation (OwningBusinessUnitReadBackFailed) rather than propagating
      unlogged. R2 — removed rendered sentence content from the leftover-placeholder exception message; added
      sentence_template_invalid as a logged+metered refusal. R3 — OntologyWriterDataverseClient no longer uses
      Lazy(PublicationOnly) (which let a burst of concurrent failures each attempt+log independently); replaced
      with a double-checked lock, cache-on-success-only field; the class is now IDisposable (disposes the
      ServiceClient; DI disposes the singleton at shutdown); a not-ready ServiceClient is disposed before
      throwing. R4 — spec.md's ADR-028 row rewritten to the accurate rule text; APPROVED marker kept. R5 —
      renamed RecordOwnershipAcrossBusinessUnits to the real org-setting key EnableOwnershipAcrossBusinessUnits
      everywhere. R7/R8 — added a distinct connect_failed reason; fixed a double-log/meter risk for one
      token-provider failure during connect (the SDK swallows that exception internally; a local flag now
      prevents the IsReady check from logging it a second time). R9 — test fakes now throw TYPED
      FaultException&lt;OrganizationServiceFault&gt; with the correct ErrorCodes (0x80060892 duplicate-key,
      0x80040220 access-denied — 0x80040299 was mislabelled in the first rework). R10 (seam) — cleanup now
      sweeps by sprk_policycode, not just tracked ids; the seam fails fast if SIGNALS_LIVE_CALLER_ID is unset;
      the BU assertion now reads the matter's BU independently rather than comparing the writer's own value to
      itself. R12 — added invariant I-12 (renumbered I-14, I-15, then I-16 on 2026-10-07/08 after master merges) to DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md §5. R13 — checked;
      sprk_regardingrecordnumber and sprk_privilegeflagged are NOT set by this writer, documented as a gap with
      citations (neither spec.md/design.md nor the canonical TodoRegardingBuilder reference assigns their
      population to this task). R14 — the previously-unused _logger field is now used in Dispose(). R6 (the
      coordinator's own investigation) — progress notes reworded per the exact instruction, not
      self-explained. R11 — a STALE banner now marks the first-draft sections; test counts below are the
      verified final numbers.
    </summary>
